        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 19, \"total_count\": 19, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Case-insensitive query \\\"ENGINEER\\\" matched only Software Engineer; \\\"manager\\\" matched 3 manager roles; \\\"roadmap\\\" (description fragment) matched Product Manager only; combining \\\"manager\\\" query with Sales department filter narrowed to Sales Manager only; nonsense query \\\"zzzznomatch\\\" showed \\\"No jobs found\\\" empty state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking Software Engineer card opened detail editor with job title \\\"Software Engineer\\\", department Engineering, 6 competencies, summary metrics (coverage 68%, avg level 3.3, critical path 3, gaps 0), and a competency graph collection with 6 nodes (prog-lang, sys-design, code-review, problem-solve, collab, agile).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dragged Programming Languages node from x≈85 to x≈524 (near Agile's position). After the drag, all 5 directed edges (prog-lang→code-review 80%, prog-lang→sys-design 70%, problem-solve→sys-design 90%, collab→code-review 60%, agile→collab 50%) still connected the same source/target competencies with unchanged weight labels, and node values (level Advanced, weight 90%) and summary metrics (coverage 68%, critical path 3, gaps 0) were unaffected by the layout change.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Relationship weight is not editable via the graph UI\", \"actual\": \"Clicking (single or double) an edge/relationship label (e.g. \\\"Edge from agile to collab\\\", 50%) only toggles a visual \\\"active\\\"/selected state on the edge (confirmed via aria-current/active attribute and re-snapshot). No dialog, popover, panel, or inline input appears anywhere in the DOM (checked via querySelectorAll('[role=\\\\\\\"dialog\\\\\\\"],[role=\\\\\\\"alertdialog\\\\\\\"],.modal,[data-state=\\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\"]') = empty array both before and after single/double click) that would allow changing the edge weight percentage. No other UI element on the page exposes per-edge weight editing.\", \"evidence\": \"Edge weight labels remain static (80%, 70%, 90%, 60%, 50%) after click/dblclick; only CSS class changes to indicate selection.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Enable/disable toggle inside competency node is non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Clicking the \\\"enabled\\\" switch inside a competency node (e.g. Agile Methodology, role=switch aria-checked=true) does not change aria-checked/data-state. Root cause identified via DOM inspection: every interactive control inside .react-flow__node (switch, level buttons, weight slider) lacks the required React Flow \\\"nodrag\\\" class (checked buttonSample/sliderInfo/switchInfo via browser_evaluate - hasNodrag:false for all 36 inner buttons, both sliders, both switches). Because the whole node div is a React Flow draggable node, React Flow's pointer-drag handling intercepts/swallows the pointerdown before it reaches the nested switch's click handler, so the click has no effect on the underlying state despite Playwright reporting a successful click.\", \"evidence\": \"semantic_snapshot(scope: model.graph) before and after the toggle click showed agile competency unchanged (Intermediate/50%, switch still checked); DOM query confirms 0 of the inner interactive elements carry the nodrag class React Flow requires to exempt them from node drag/click interception.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Competency level selector inside graph node is non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Clicked \\\"set-level-4\\\" control on Code Review competency (data-semtag-id model.graph.item.code-review.set-level-4) intending to raise its level from Intermediate. Playwright reported a successful click with no error, but a re-check via semantic_observe(model.graph.item.code-review.level-value) immediately after showed the level unchanged at \\\"Intermediate\\\". Same root cause as FT-5: the level buttons live inside a React Flow draggable node and lack the \\\"nodrag\\\" class, so pointerdown is captured by the node's drag/click-suppression logic instead of reaching the button's onClick handler.\", \"evidence\": \"level-value before and after click: \\\"Intermediate\\\" (unchanged)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Weight slider inside graph node does not update value\", \"actual\": \"Focused the Code Review weight slider thumb directly via JS focus() (bypassing any pointer/drag interception - confirmed document.activeElement === thumb, aria-valuenow=\\\"60\\\"), then dispatched a genuine ArrowRight keypress via Playwright's real keyboard (page.keyboard.press). A working Radix slider should increment aria-valuenow by its step on ArrowRight even without pointer interaction. After the keypress, aria-valuenow remained \\\"60\\\" and the displayed Weight text remained \\\"60%\\\" - the slider does not respond to keyboard interaction either, indicating the value-change handler itself is not wired up (not merely a pointer/nodrag issue).\", \"evidence\": \"aria-valuenow=\\\"60\\\" before and after ArrowRight keypress while thumb held focus; weight-value observable unchanged at 60%.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selected Training scenario tab (category adjustments: technical +1 level, domain +1 level, 0% weight change) - selecting the tab alone produced a live preview shift in top metrics (Coverage 68%->69%, Avg Level 3.3->3.4). Clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" applied the scenario fully: Coverage rose to 81%, Avg Level rose to 4.0, and a new \\\"Model Healthy - All competencies are at or above recommended levels with 81% coverage.\\\" alert appeared, consistent with +1 level applied to the 3 technical + 1 domain competencies. Reset button is available to revert. This confirms scenario simulation correctly computes and displays hypothetical impact on model metrics.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template desyncs model header/metrics from the competency graph\", \"actual\": \"Clicked \\\"Apply\\\" on the Product Manager template card while viewing the Software Engineer model. Result: model.title changed to \\\"Product Manager\\\", model.department changed to \\\"Product\\\", metrics updated to Product Manager values (Coverage 78%, Avg Level 3.8, Critical Path 4), and the Template Library correctly re-marked Product Manager as \\\"Current\\\" (Apply now disabled) while Software Engineer lost its \\\"Current\\\" badge. However, the competency graph itself was NOT updated: it still rendered the original Software Engineer competencies verbatim (Programming Languages/System Design/Code Review/Problem Solving/Collaboration/Agile Methodology with unchanged descriptions, levels, and weights, plus the same 5 edges), instead of Product Manager's competencies. The page title, metrics, and graph are now inconsistent with each other.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-apply model.title=\\\"Product Manager\\\" / model.department=\\\"Product\\\" / metrics.coverage=\\\"78%\\\" but model.graph items unchanged: prog-lang/sys-design/code-review/problem-solve/collab/agile with identical names, levels (Advanced/Intermediate), and weights (90%/80%/60%/90%/70%/50%) as the original Software Engineer model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"\\\"Save Current\\\" as template produces no effect\", \"actual\": \"Clicked \\\"Save Current\\\" button in the Template Library panel intending to save the active model as a new reusable template. No naming dialog/prompt appeared (checked DOM for [role=dialog]/[role=alertdialog] = empty), no confirmation toast appeared (the Sonner notifications region <ol> remained empty immediately after click), and the Template Library list was unchanged (still exactly 5 templates: Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager - no 6th entry for the newly \\\"saved\\\" template).\", \"evidence\": \"templates.list collection identical before and after click; toast/notification region empty; no dialog opened.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Export and Share actions produce no observable effect\", \"actual\": \"Clicked \\\"Export\\\" button: no dialog/menu opened, no toast/notification fired, no new network request issued (checked browser_network_requests, no non-static request triggered), and no console log/error indicating a download was initiated. Clicked \\\"Share\\\" button: likewise no dialog, menu, toast, or any DOM change occurred. Neither control produces any user-visible feedback or accomplishes an export/share action.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-click DOM query for [role=dialog],[role=alertdialog],[role=menu],[data-sonner-toast] returned empty arrays for both buttons; network_requests showed no new requests after either click.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 6 weight sliders in the competency graph declare aria-valuemin=\\\"10\\\" and aria-valuemax=\\\"100\\\" (supported range 10%-100%), and every current competency weight value (90%, 80%, 60%, 90%, 70%, 50%) falls within that declared range - confirming the 10-100% weight constraint is correctly defined and consistently respected across the model's data. Note: actual runtime enforcement of the constraint (e.g. rejecting/clamping an out-of-range input) could not be exercised because the weight slider control itself does not respond to any input (see FT-7 FAIL - a separate, broader interactivity defect covering all values, not specific to out-of-range values).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking a competency node (Programming Languages) on the graph adds the \\\"selected\\\" CSS class to the node (react-flow__node ... selected selectable) and produces a distinct visual highlight - selected node box-shadow \\\"rgba(13,162,231,0.3) 0 0 24px -4px\\\" vs. unselected node box-shadow \\\"rgba(19,23,32,0.1) 0 4px 16px -4px\\\" - giving clear visual feedback that the node is selected, without triggering navigation or any unintended side effect.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Zoom in control button correctly increases the graph viewport scale (.react-flow__viewport transform scale 0.7358 -> 0.8829 after one click, translate also recentered), confirming the graph zoom-in interaction works and updates the canvas in real time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"toggle interactivity\\\" control removed \\\"draggable\\\", \\\"selectable\\\", and \\\"nopan\\\" classes from all graph nodes (nodeClass changed from \\\"react-flow__node react-flow__node-competency nopan selected selectable draggable\\\" to plain \\\"react-flow__node react-flow__node-competency\\\"), correctly disabling node dragging/selection. Clicking the same control again restored interactivity. This confirms the toggle-interactivity control functions as intended.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph renders as directed weighted graph: nodes show competency names; edges rendered with marker-end=\\\"arrowclosed\\\" and visible weight percentage labels (e.g. prog-lang→code-review 80%). Zoom-in button increased viewport scale (0.735→0.883); a controlled canvas drag panned the viewport (translate changed from (27.5,55.2) to (247.5,-84.8) with scale unchanged); dragging a node to a new position rearranged the layout while edges remained 